Changes on branch k2/0.28 (from tag v0.28.0):
- yrs (hardening): stricter limits when decoding. Tests in yrs/tests/decode_prealloc.rs.
- yrs: `Doc::transact_mut_as(client)`: a transaction on the doc whose changes are made as another
  client (new blocks and redone items take that client's ID and next clocks); the doc's own ID
  is restored at commit, before subdocs added in it are given an ID, and on a panic. Tests in
  yrs/tests/transact_mut_as.rs and the undo manager's unit tests.
- yrs: a position index for text: per-branch (index, ID) markers, resolved by ID lookup, kept by
  local text inserts and removals and dropped on any other change; used only by texts without
  formatting; a sampled shadow walk (Doc::set_position_shadow_rate) checks it and reports a
  mismatch to Doc::set_position_audit_hook. Tests in yrs/tests/position_index.rs and the
  position_index unit tests.
- yrs: the undo manager restores items in a deterministic order (as Yjs does). Test in the
  undo manager's unit tests.
- yrs (hardening): more robust handling of updates that arrive out of order. Tests in
  yrs/tests/pending_retry.rs.
- yrs: encoded bytes don't depend on hash order. Tests in yrs/tests/deterministic_bytes.rs.
- yrs (tests): the fuzz harness (test_utils.rs) is deterministic: its peer and message maps are
  ordered, a scenario's seed comes from YRS_FUZZ_SEED (random if unset, printed either way),
  and the final check requires that no peer has a pending update or delete set.
- yrs: `Update::has_subdoc_content()`: a decode-only check of whether an update carries subdocument
  content, so an embedder that never uses subdocuments can refuse such updates before applying
  them. Tests in yrs/tests/subdoc_content.rs.
- yrs: a transaction's work is proportional to the clients it touches, not to every client the
  doc has seen. It records the clients it pushes a block for (item, GC or skip) with each one's
  state vector entry before the first; nested-type change tracking, map/XML event keys, the
  transaction's encoded update and the update observers' change check look at those clients
  only, instead of building the whole before state, state vector and after state. The full
  before_state()/after_state() are still built on request and list the same clients upstream's
  did. New: TransactionMut::before_clock/after_clock/touched_clients. A test-only oracle
  (Doc::set_full_state_vectors) keeps upstream's path. Tests in yrs/tests/touched_clients.rs.
- yrs (hardening): stricter handling of rarely used content. Tests included.
- yrs (hardening): v2 encoding fix. Test in yrs/tests/v2_skip.rs.
- yrs (hardening): more complete transaction updates. A test-only feature (planted-relay-bug)
  restores the previous behaviour for tests. Tests in yrs/tests/update_event_relay.rs.
- yrs (hardening): stricter handling when applying updates. Test in yrs/tests/gc_split.rs.
- yrs (hardening): garbage-collection robustness. Tests included.
- yrs: builds warning-free under RUSTFLAGS='-D warnings' (default features, `weak` and the
  test-only planted-* features), with no change in behaviour.
